    >[=] Choose one mutable action model for occurrence-aware transactions =occurrence-model-owner $NEEDS DECISION: which public model owns mutable actions, Workspace or TransactionModel?
    Deferred 4#4 from review 20261102-030308/4 by launcher decision in fix run 20261102-030308; no preferred option. Finding: Occurrence resolution keeps a second, separately loaded copy of the workspace (occurrence_transaction_input) in sync with the transaction model by copying every action across after each operation, then copies the charter's actions back by matching a built charters/<file> path string. Source-file writes from the occurrence batch are then filtered out. Two in-memory copies of the same files are reconciled by hand on every operation, and an inconsistency check papers over the gap. The runbook says this kind of second read must be fixed or escalated as NEEDS DECISION, not shipped. The fold should work on a single model.
    Measured code: filesystem::transition_action and transact load TransactionModel/FileState and fold close/reopen/update through prepare_native_transaction and transaction::apply_one; archive/unarchive instead use shared prepare_action_move (with transaction::tree_root), not apply_one. Thus the close/reopen/archive/transact writers already have shared paths, but not literally one transaction fold for archive. TransactionModel owns Vec<FileState> with active/completed Vec<Action>, expected revisions and dirty flags; Workspace owns charters with sourced actions, plans and hydrated links. occurrence_transaction_input loads Workspace separately. prepare_transaction_with_occurrences copies model actions into Workspace preserving plan_id/external_occurrence_key, runs fold_materialized_occurrence_resolution, copies actions back by charters/<file>, filters duplicate source writes, and rejects inconsistent preconditions. The occurrence fold reads charter plans and hydrated links, freezes snapshots, clears live links, stages a next token through stage_prepared_plan_token and relinks sidecars through link_staged_occurrences; it also maintains Plan resources and sync-store evidence.
    Option A: Workspace owns mutable actions. Adapt transaction FileState/apply_one/expand_cascade/rendering to mutate the loaded charter action lists directly, retain completed-file evidence and dirty tracking without a second action vector, route native transaction loading through that one workspace read, and align prepare_action_move with the same owner. The occurrence helpers can continue using charter plans and sourced actions. These are identified change sites, not an effort estimate.
    Option B: TransactionModel owns mutable actions. Refactor occurrence folding plus stage_prepared_plan_token/link_staged_occurrences to consume transaction file actions and separate charter-plan/hydrated-link metadata; load actions once with revisions, use explicit charter-to-resource identities rather than formatted path matching, and emit source writes only from that owner. Keep Plan/store/sidecar evidence separate without duplicating action lists. Adapting remaining Workspace-based sync consumers may also be needed (guess; not measured).
    Do not start consolidation before Darrion chooses. Independent 4#1/4#3 fixes and dead-API removal for 4#2 are committed separately in this run. The existing close-individually and ci-core actions are not completed or blocked by this deferral.$ +human ^2026-11-02T04:05 #01a19a6f-794d-77f1-9f00-13246c009cc7
